{"title":"2024 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Glen, Hao, Ioana, Julia, Karla, and Levi participated in the 2023 Canadian Team Mathematics Contest. On their team uniforms, each had a different number chosen from the list <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Hao’s and Julia’s numbers were even. Karla’s and Levi’s numbers were prime numbers. Glen’s number was a perfect square. What was Ioana’s number?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/9/e999365b9aed9b8d20c3eb31f558fcfe5421c476.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 11 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 15 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 14 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 13 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"433\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can eliminate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> as Ioana's number because they were the only two <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Prime_number\" title=\"Prime number\">prime numbers</a> in the list, and both Karla's and Levi's numbers were prime.\n</p><p>Next, we can eliminate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> as Iona's number because it was the only <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perfect_square\" title=\"Perfect square\">perfect square</a> of the numbers in the list, and Glen's number was a perfect square.\n</p><p>Finally, we can eliminate both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> as Iona's numbers because they were the only two remaining even numbers in the list that haven't been eliminated yet and both Hao's and Julia's numbers are even.\n</p><p>Since all other numbers have been eliminated, Iona's number must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/d/a7d5dda7af2ae71086f2a24014985899066bda42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Pascal&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC Pascal (page does not exist)\">2024 CEMC Pascal</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Pascal_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC Pascal Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Pascal_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC Pascal Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2024 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 13 (page does not exist)\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_1